{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HX1WDuPxj5jTwpFjD4YY3L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context and propose tasks for release 05.2 (columnar operations pair: cut, paste).\n\nFrom the analysis:\n- Release 05.2 has two use cases: rel05.2-uc001-cut and rel05.2-uc002-paste\n- Both have specstatus: spec_complete, codestatus: not started\n- I need to look at what PRDs exist for these\n\nThe recent commit shows: \"Task 354: Implement cmd/cut -- prd-cut R1-R4: selection modes, delimiters, file handling, exit codes\"\n\nSo cmd/cut was already implemented in the most recent commit! Let me check - the git status shows we're on branch `generation-gh-336-generate-code-r05.2` and the most recent commit is `0fb74de Task 354: Implement cmd/cut`.\n\n\nSince cut is already complete, I'll focus on proposing the paste implementation task. I'm limited to one task maximum, so I'll reference the paste PRD and outline what the implementation should cover based on the standard paste command features like delimiter configuration and serial mode options. Looking at the recent cut implementation as a reference, I should follow that same pattern and propose a single task covering paste's core requirements along with tests, rather than splitting them across multiple tasks.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27549,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27549},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82a22c1b-c416-4701-a5e6-98d1951bbe11","uuid":"0f2bf373-a083-413a-acd4-91162698d132"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HX1WDuPxj5jTwpFjD4YY3L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils stress-tests an AI code generation pipeline by regenerating GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Human writes PRDs/use-cases; mage-claude-orchestrator generates Go code in `cmd/` and `pkg/`; `pkg/testutils` runs differential tests comparing Go binaries against GNU references.\n\n**Current state:** Specifications complete through rel05.4. Code generation is on branch `generation-gh-336-generate-code-r05.2`. The most recent commit (`0fb74de`) implemented `cmd/cut` (Task 354, prd-cut R1-R4). That leaves **paste** as the remaining use case in rel05.2.\n\n**Current release:** rel05.2 — columnar operations pair (cut, paste). Cut is done. Paste remains.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 05.2 has two use cases. `rel05.2-uc001-cut` was just completed. `rel05.2-uc002-paste` is the only remaining task. Paste has no code dependencies beyond the existing `pkg/sys` (for SIGPIPE handling) and `pkg/testutils` (for differential tests), both already implemented.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/paste -- prd-paste R1-R4: parallel merge, serial mode, delimiters, file handling\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd-paste.yaml (all requirements for paste)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.2-uc002-paste.yaml (end-to-end execution path)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.2.yaml (test cases for paste)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared protocols: differential testing, SIGPIPE handling, graceful skip)\n      - cmd/cut/main.go (peer implementation in same release for patterns and style)\n      - cmd/cut/cut_test.go (peer test file for differential test patterns)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests API)\n      - pkg/sys/signal.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler API)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/paste/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: paste implementation -- parallel merge, serial mode, delimiter cycling, stdin/file handling\n      - path: cmd/paste/paste_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gpaste reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement parallel merge mode (default): read one line from each input file per output line, join with delimiter, output to stdout. When a file is exhausted, substitute empty string for its field.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement serial mode (-s/--serial): for each input file, join all its lines into a single output line using the delimiter list, cycling delimiters as needed.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement delimiter list (-d/--delimiters): accept a string of delimiter characters, cycle through them for successive fields on the same output line, reset to the first delimiter for each new output line. Support backslash escapes: \\\\n (newline), \\\\t (tab), \\\\\\\\ (backslash), \\\\0 (empty string).\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement file handling: accept multiple file operands, treat - as stdin (only one stdin stream shared across all - operands), read from stdin when no operands given. Exit 0 on success, exit 1 on error with diagnostic to stderr. Handle --help and --version flags.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main, matching the shared protocol in ARCHITECTURE.yaml.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Default delimiter is TAB when -d is not specified, matching GNU paste behavior.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use bufio.Scanner for line-by-line reading. Track EOF state per input independently so parallel mode continues until all inputs are exhausted.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Differential tests call exec.LookPath for gpaste and t.Skip if not found, matching the graceful-skip shared protocol.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/paste/main.go compiles with no errors via go build ./cmd/paste/.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Parallel merge mode joins lines from multiple files with TAB delimiter by default.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Serial mode (-s) joins all lines of each file into one output line.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Delimiter cycling works correctly with multi-character delimiter lists and backslash escapes.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Stdin is handled as - operand and as default when no files given.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/paste/ passes with gpaste as reference binary (or skips gracefully if gpaste not in PATH).\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"Exit code is 0 on success, 1 on error with diagnostic to stderr.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27549,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27549},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82a22c1b-c416-4701-a5e6-98d1951bbe11","uuid":"71d80d91-8a54-4003-9b43-8d7bd2159085"}
